# Veripsa release gate (auto-discovered). One gate per file -> two PRs adding gates add two FILES, never a
# shared line -> no false merge conflict on registration. register_gate is defined in run_gates.sh.
# Format: register_gate <test> <marker> <name> <ok_blurb> <desc> [tail]
# GATE-HYGIENE: description strings must contain NO dollar-sign and NO backtick (set -u in the runner).
register_gate "tests/test_cross_substrate_openapi.py" "OPENAPI SUBSTRATE GATE: PASS" "OpenAPI/Swagger REST cross-substrate coupling: spec operations + schemas referenced from backend handlers and frontend clients" "openapi substrate: spec operationId/path operations + component schemas couple to anchored references (backend def of operationId + frontend path literal, crown-jewel, no code edge); marker-gate: plain yaml/json without an openapi/swagger marker mint NO api_operation/api_schema nodes; precision: generic paths (/health) + generic schema names (Error) + comment-only mentions do NOT couple; param-style normalization: /users/{id} couples to /users/:id and /users/{userId}; json spec + Swagger 2 definitions parsed the same way; never-crash: empty + malformed + binary-ish specs do not raise; content-free: a description/example value or a secret never appears in graph output; additive: pure-Python repo with ordinary config json/yaml gets zero api_ nodes (no config regression); line-scanner fallback: a yaml spec still yields operations + schemas with PyYAML absent." "OpenAPI/Swagger REST cross-substrate: a REST operation (operationId getUserById, or a normalized GET /users/{} from path+method) or a component schema DEFINED in an openapi.yaml/.json spec and IMPLEMENTED by a backend handler whose function is named after the operationId and CALLED by a frontend client with a /users/:id route literal are coupled via a shared api_operation/api_schema node with NO import/call edge. A file is treated as a spec ONLY when its parsed top level carries openapi:/swagger:, so ordinary yaml/json stays in the config pass. Two-pass known-set discipline emits queries only for anchored references to known operations/schemas. Precision guards stoplist generic paths and schema names and strip comments. YAML uses the explicit production PyYAML dependency, while this substrate keeps its bounded line-scanner fallback so its own extraction remains fail-soft; JSON uses the stdlib. Content-free and bounded. Gate 132." 9
